# msuiter valgrind-suppressations file -- deliberately, verifiably EMPTY.
#
# Doctrine: no violation is ever silenced by this file. Ownership of an
# observed report is adjudicated in run_valgrind_leg.sh's census layer --
# where the allowances are code, carry evidence citations, and are
# regression-tested by the census_fixture battery. A suppression file can
# do none of that on this fork, for two measured reasons (2026-10-21
# control probes):
#
#   1. The renamed fork's suppression matcher is dead. A textbook
#      invalid-read violation is suppressed by ZERO entries under every
#      accepted spelling -- the { opener, the tool prefix, fun:/obj:
#      frames alike. Entries parse, are counted, and never bind.
#   2. The legacy "Memcheck:" prefix in the original grammar is FATAL
#      here: valgrind exits "unknown tool suppression type". This file's
#      pre-#45 header taught that illegal prefix -- a trap for whoever
#      added an entry in good faith. The prefix this fork accepts is
#      "Valgrind:", and it must be spelled exactly that way:
#
#        {
#        name=<label>
#        Valgrind:<kind-of-error>
#        ...fun:/obj: frame lines...
#        }
#
# Because matching is dead, an entry here could not silence anything even
# if authored -- which is precisely why it must stay empty: a growing
# suppressions file would advertise protection that does not exist. The
# census refuses any report that claims (suppressed: N) with N > 0
# (NO SELF-DECEPTION law), so leaning on this file reddens the leg loudly.
#
# R ships no valgrind.supp of its own: falsified 2026-10-21 against the
# R 4.6.1 source tarball (full listing, zero valgrind hits). Distro
# packages maintain their own; this file is ours and remains a zero-entry
# attestation of that fact.
